// ============================================================================
// 03 - Write attempts (POST / PUT) in a window
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Purpose : isolate the requests that could actually CHANGE something -
//           uploads, logins, form posts, webshell drops. CsBytes is the
//           request body size: a large POST to an odd path is a likely upload.
// Use it  : same window as query 02, but stripped down to the dangerous verbs.
//           Cross-check any 2xx/3xx here - a *successful* write from a
//           suspicious IP is the finding that matters.
// Table   : AppServiceHTTPLogs
//
// TUNABLES:
//   datetime window        -> widen/narrow as needed
//   in ("POST", "PUT")     -> add "PATCH", "DELETE"; or use
//                             `!in ("GET","HEAD","OPTIONS")` to catch verb abuse
//   add `| where ScStatus < 400`  -> only writes that SUCCEEDED
//   add `| where CsBytes > 10000` -> only large bodies (file uploads)
// ============================================================================
AppServiceHTTPLogs
| where TimeGenerated between (datetime(2026-09-02 00:00) .. datetime(2026-09-02 00:30))
| where CsMethod in ("POST", "PUT")
| project TimeGenerated, CIp, CsUriStem, CsUriQuery, ScStatus, CsBytes, UserAgent
| sort by TimeGenerated asc
